<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mitinti of Ashdod</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 700 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mitinti of Ashdod was king of the Philistine city of Ashdod around 700 BCE. He appears in the annals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sennacherib">Sennacherib</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> among the western rulers who brought tribute during the campaign of 701 BCE. Having stayed loyal to Assyria while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hezekiah">Hezekiah</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> rebelled, he received a share of the Judahite towns that Sennacherib took from Hezekiah.</p></div>
